{title: O Jesus, Thou Art Standing}
{artist: William W. How / Justin H. Knecht}
{genre: Hymn}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Response}
{key: D}
{key_original: Eb}
{tempo: 115}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (The Hymnbook (Richmond, Virginia: Presbyterian Church in the United States, 1955), # 266. Begins with same measures as Knecht’s tune Kocher)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D7]O Jesus, Thou art standing,
[D7]Outside the [G]fast closed [A]door,
[D7]In lowly patience wait[G]ing
[D]To [Em]pass [G]the [F#m]threshold [D]o’er:
[D]Shame [Bm]on us, Christian bro[Em]thers,
[Em]His [E7]name and sign who [A]bear,
[D]O shame, thrice shame upon [G]us,
[D]To [Em]keep [G]Him [A]standing [D]there!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D7]O Jesus, Thou art knocking;
[D7]And lo, that [G]hand is [A]scarred,
[D7]And thorns Thy brow encir[G]cle,
[D]And [Em]tears [G]Thy [F#m]face have [D]marred:
[D]O [Bm]love that passeth know[Em]ledge,
[Em]So [E7]patiently to [A]wait!
[D]O sin that hath no eq[G]ual,
[D]So [Em]fast [G]to [A]bar the [D]gate!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D7]O Jesus, Thou art pleading
[D7]In accents [G]meek and [A]low,
[D7]I died for you, My child[G]ren,
[D]And [Em]will [G]you [F#m]treat Me [D]so?
[D]O [Bm]Lord, with shame and sor[Em]row
[Em]We [E7]open now the [A]door;
[D]Dear Savior, enter, en[G]ter,
[D]And [Em]leave [G]us [A]never[D]more.
{end_of_verse}
